int bc_debug_remove_breakpoint(bc_client_t *c, int bp_id);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes a single breakpoint from the debugger by its ID.
The function sends a \f[CR]remove_breakpoint\f[R] request on
\f[CR]CHAN_DEBUG\f[R] (channel 4) and waits for the server\(cqs
acknowledgement.
.PP
The breakpoint ID is the value returned by a previous call to
\f[CR]bc_debug_add_breakpoint()\f[R].
Once removed, the breakpoint no longer triggers and its ID is never
reused.
.PP
If the removed breakpoint was the last one and the debugger is in
\f[CR]\(dqrun\(dq\f[R] mode, the debug pre\-command hook remains
registered (the debugger is still enabled).
Use \f[CR]bc_debug_disable()\f[R] to fully deactivate the debugger.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]c\f[R] \(em Pointer to an authenticated \f[CR]bc_client_t\f[R]
connection.
Must not be NULL.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]bp_id\f[R] \(em The breakpoint ID to remove.
Must be a positive integer previously returned by
\f[CR]bc_debug_add_breakpoint()\f[R].
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \f[CR]BC_OK\f[R] (0) on success.
.PP
