.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Breakpoint IDs are never reused.
Once removed, the same ID cannot be added back.
.IP \(bu 2
Removing a breakpoint while execution is stopped at that breakpoint is
valid.
The command will proceed normally on the next
\f[CR]bc_debug_continue()\f[R] or \f[CR]bc_debug_step()\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
To remove all breakpoints at once, use \f[CR]bc_debug_disable()\f[R]
followed by \f[CR]bc_debug_enable()\f[R], or iterate over the list from
\f[CR]bc_debug_list_breakpoints()\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
Thread safety: the client library is not thread\-safe.
